"note": "Sortiraparis (citing Le Parisien), Affiches Parisiennes (09:53) and Paris Rouge all report the Gilets Jaunes and union march leaving République at 14:00, which matches the Gilets Jaunes call (Aladom). Student and high-school groups also gather here. Police used tear gas at République around 12:38 with several hundred people already gathered (BFMTV, via Titres de presse), and groups heading here put up barricades from street barriers around 12:30 (Le Tribunal du Net). The prefecture counted 133 arrests in Paris at 14:00, mostly for groups gathering to commit violence or damage (Humanité). Authorities expected 30,000 to 60,000 people in Paris (Anadolu). The march then started from here despite tensions with police (franceinfo live headline). Clashes and wild processions in Paris are also reported (Epoch Times FR headline), without locations I could read.",
